From da1724f71f5c7803fc1a628f3daab96f7a2023ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: andesk <build@andesk.local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:57:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] patches: WebRTC signalling needs a rendezvous key exchange in
 hbbs

Upstream's controlled peer emits NO WebRTC signalling (SDP answer, ICE
candidates) until the rendezvous server has run a key exchange:
rendezvous_mediator.rs:718 and :950 call secure_tcp_required and DROP the
signalling on failure rather than send it in the clear. Upstream hbbs has never
implemented that exchange (git log --all -SKeyExchange -- src/ is empty), so
WebRTC cannot work against a self-hosted server at all: the peer builds a valid
answer, fails to encrypt the leg carrying it, and falls back to the relay.

Three changes, all in hbbs.

1. Key exchange (accept_key_exchange). The server speaks first. A peer that
   secures a connection blocks waiting for our KeyExchange and sends nothing,
   while a controller speaks first, so a connection silent for 500ms gets one
   offered. Signs KX_PARAMS_DOMAIN + KxParams{our ephemeral X25519 pk,
   version 0} with the hbbs Ed25519 key, then opens the sealed symmetric key the
   peer returns. Both directions then run secretbox (BytesCodec::set_crypt_key,
   nonce = per-direction incrementing LE u64). Only version 0 (one key both
   ways) is offered: this tree's hbb_common predates v1, and the client's
   kx_version_for picks the lower of the two.

2. PunchHoleResponse and RelayResponse must carry webrtc_sdp_answer. Upstream
   copies neither field, so the answer never reaches the controller.

3. The IceCandidate branch must return true, and trickled candidates must use a
   send that does not take the controller's sink out of tcp_punch
   (send_to_tcp_keep). Upstream returns the default false, which breaks the read
   loop and closes the controller's socket after the first candidate; plain
   send_to_tcp removes the sink, stranding every later candidate.

Supporting schema and codec work, also here:
  libs/hbb_common/protos/rendezvous.proto  KeyExchange.version and
      .signed_params, plus a new KxParams. KeyExchange is already at field 25
      upstream, so no field renumbering.
  libs/hbb_common/src/tcp.rs               KX_PARAMS_DOMAIN
  libs/hbb_common/src/bytes_codec.rs       read and write secretbox for a
      secured connection

This tree's hbb_common cannot simply be bumped to the newer upstream that has
these helpers: 1ee667e..229b904 removes about 4900 lines (fs.rs, message.proto
and platform/* move to other crates), so the exchange is implemented here
against the older submodule.
